From a6cec9d71f1cb2fff75b46545cab2dd85944fe30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] avalanche: add quorum node-count and circulating-supply
 activation gates

Enforce organic Avalanche quorum node-count and staked circulating-supply
activation gates.

Original-Commit: 14192312769a7fda2627d1ec29dc91eef039bb6c
Original-Patch: v2/023
Split-Concern: whole

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Introduce native-only quorum node/supply parameters, original stake accounting and native fixture at their actual V2 owner, preserving the coherent shared quorum generation and upstream reward side effects. Omit duplicate adaptive/batch implementations, visitors, option definitions and independent atomic updater already supplied by shared owners. Original native gate behavior is retained; no new regression or timing in this application pass.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Absorb duplicate-only cleanup at first native quorum owner: keep one original quorum fixture (all unique assertions retained) and omit the unused query-timeout local. The later124 restoration/removal mailbox is redundant once earlier batches/visitors/options are retained once.
(cherry picked from commit 00863dfe20ef966dbad1b00da08bd5a4122a7596)

Canonical-Source-Commit: 00863dfe20ef966dbad1b00da08bd5a4122a7596

Coordinator integration provenance (metrics369):
Retain native const quorum eligibility API and configured minQuorumNodes, with read-only metric latch observation using that minimum.
All build/runtime/observer controls deferred by user compile-first policy; ordered source replay is not runtime approval.

Coordinator integration provenance (network403):
Union appended relay command names with existing native Treasury/AVABATCH protocol tables; numeric native ID table preservation is separately proved append-only.
Original scripted commands/hashes above are original-author provenance; modified parent/tool/catalog hashes are not claimed to reproduce this composition. Exact coordinator adaptation scripts and ordered tree proof are in composed403-network-metrics-delivery. Build/runtime/benchmarks NOT_RUN for this composition under user compile-first policy.

Coordinator integration provenance (reference405):
Preserve earlier purposeful source repairs through downstream consumer/context adaptations; exact conflict ledger retained.
All60 authored input payloads retained, with prerequisite-aware same-purpose splits; distinct legacy-index and inherited CXX compatibility remain independent. Pre-format source equals exact403+all60 control tree95718fceff83364b74294a751bd752b2f1a4e384. Only pinnedRuff import/format cleanup follows. Original author commands/hashes are historical reference evidence, not combined405 approval. Reference OFF/native/Rust full gates are preserved separately; combined compile/runtime NOT_RUN.

Coordinator causal native prerequisite repair (2026-10-20):
Native consensus112 introduces a const-policy quorum eligibility caller; introduce the actual later124 logically-const latch prerequisite with it. Mutable atomic only; no threshold/supply changes.
Declare the later124 const quorum eligibility overload at first native112 caller; keep old nonconst staking-sideeffect API unchanged. Later active-tip lock annotation stays with124 where that lock exists.
Split only the later124 const eligibility implementation to first consumer112: retain existing fixed8node threshold, score/IBD/proof eligibility and atomic latch. Exclude later configured min-node/supply branches until124; no const_cast, nonconst sideeffects, policy bypass or new algorithm. Later124 keeps exact final implementation/wrapper.
Exact original failed native compilation and one diagnostic inventory are retained. This is an introduced-defect/API-consumer fix, not a new purpose. Final source tree and507count remain unchanged; rootbenchmarkworker owns repairedprefix compilation.

